<title>USA: CME July lumber futures fall $10 limit late.</title>
<headline>CME July lumber futures fall $10 limit late.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-05-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>CME lumber futures fell the $10.00 per thousand board feet limit in late trade as commission house selling triggered sell stops, floor sources said.</p>
<p>Dealers said heavy stops were hit around $387.20 on the July contract, which was offered the $10 limit down at $382.60. Other months were down $9.20 to up $0.10 at 1302 CDT.</p>
<p>Cash lumber trade was quiet after weakness late last week.</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk 312-408-8720))</p>
</text>
